According to a new report from Intel Market Research, the global Software & System Modeling Tools market was valued at USD 6.1 billion in 2025 and is projected to rise from USD 6.3 billion in 2026 to USD 9.8 billion by 2034, reflecting a compound annual growth rate of approximately 5.7% over the forecast horizon. This upward momentum is driven by the expanding adoption of model based systems engineering (MBSE) across aerospace, automotive, and industrial automation, alongside rising investment in digital twin initiatives and increasingly stringent regulatory requirements for safety critical systems.
Software & system modeling tools enable engineers and developers to create abstract representations of software architectures, system behaviours, and business processes using standards such as UML (Unified Modeling Language) and SysML (Systems Modeling Language). These platforms support simulation, validation, and documentation activities that reduce design errors and accelerate time to market for complex products ranging from embedded devices to enterprise applications.
